    "accuracy_limitation_explanation": "In predictive maintenance for server room cooling equipment, failure events within the next 24 hours are relatively uncommon compared to normal operating intervals (typically 10-15% positive prevalence in this dataset, and often <2% in production). A naive classifier that always predicts 'No Failure' can achieve 85-98% accuracy while missing 100% of impending failures (0% recall), leading to catastrophic thermal shutdowns. Therefore, Recall (catching real failures before overheat), Precision (avoiding alert fatigue), F1-score, PR-AUC, and Confusion Matrix analysis are essential alongside accuracy."
